    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Think of the Fourier Transform as a way to decompose a complex signal into its simpler, individual frequency components, much like breaking a chord into its single notes. Instead of looking at how a signal changes over time, this transform rephrases the data to reveal exactly which pure sine and cosine waves combine to create that specific waveform. This shift in perspective is powerful because it allows us to filter out specific frequencies or analyze system responses in ways that are impossible using only time-domain analysis.",
